<title>USA: Judge ousts Hill &amp; Knowlton from Fla. tobacco suit.</title>
<headline>Judge ousts Hill &amp; Knowlton from Fla. tobacco suit.</headline>
<dateline>WEST PALM BEACH, Fla. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The public relations firm Hill &amp; Knowlton will no longer face potential liability in Florida's $1 billion Medicaid suit against the tobacco industry, a state judge ruled Tuesday.</p>
<p>Judge Harold Cohen said the company's actions took place too far in the past for it to be considered a partner in the conspiracy to misinform the public alleged by Florida in its suit.</p>
</text>
